PARKED, not applied. Result of v1.4.0-rc2 (26 Oct 2026, direct on a FreeSync monitor,
ObsessiveRug): with VRR on, the picture shifts, blinks and scrolls; no VRR signal
detected. The HDMI bridge locks the frame timing itself, so a variable timing from
the GPU doesn't get through, with or without the FreeSync InfoFrame. VRR needs
Sony's own bridge setup, which is unknown. Kept for that day: the FreeSync
InfoFrame path (bridge slot 0x7e40) and the range parser work.

PS5 HDMI: VRR (FreeSync) through the HDMI bridge           [ps5-bazzite-deck]

Offered when the sink's EDID has an AMD FreeSync block (FLAVA3 only), used
when VRR is switched on in the desktop or Game Mode settings. No option.

1. amdgpu only offers VRR on a DP sink that may ignore the MSA timing and has
   a refresh range; the bridge reports neither, and 7.3 doesn't read the
   range of an HDMI sink behind DP. The range comes from the sink's FreeSync
   block (EDID copy bounded by the message length, taken under a lock,
   parsed from a private snapshot). Not from the HDMI Forum VRR range (HDMI
   VRR needs VTEM packets the bridge isn't known to send), not from the range
   limits descriptor (TVs list one without VRR).
2. "Ignore MSA timing" is never set on the PS5 bridge: with it, v1.4.0-rc1
   testers got no picture or a shifting one, even with VRR off.
3. Only while VRR is switched on (amdgpu's state ACTIVE_VARIABLE), the
   FreeSync InfoFrame goes out in amdgpu's HDMI layout (SPD v1: supported /
   enabled / active, min / max refresh) through the bridge's InfoFrame slot at
   0x7e40, the HDR InfoFrame's slot, so never while HDR is on. Sent again
   after every video setup and HDR InfoFrame (both rewrite the slot or its
   enable), switched off when VRR is switched off or not supported. amdgpu's
   own FreeSync SDP to the bridge is off (it would say "enabled" with VRR off).
   So with VRR switched off, nothing reaches the bridge that didn't before.
---

